  "sourceUrl": "https://docsis.org/files/C3200_datasheet_v24.pdf",
  "notes": "Casa C3200 datasheet: 3RU chassis, 'one Switch and Management Module slot and six slots for DOCSIS interface modules'. SMM = '12-port GbE copper or fiber' uplinks plus '10/100BaseT management port' and 'RS232 serial port (DB9)'. DQM16 = 16 downstream QAM channels over 4 F-type 75 ohm ports (4 channels/port, ~152 Mbps per port); DCU16 = 16 upstream channels in 8 F-type ports (2 channels/port, ~61 Mbps per port). Fully populated 3 x DQM16 + 3 x DCU16 gives the datasheet's headline 48DS x 48US density: 12 downstream and 24 upstream service-group F-connectors, each rated 100M in engine terms rather than the chassis aggregate. Category is 'modem' per batch convention - the repo's other CMTS entries (E6000, cBR-8, C100G) use 'router'."
